    yours. This is why the permission granted in section 4.1 is non-transferable
    and non-sublicensable without contradicting sections 4.1(c) and 4.2: the
    copy is passed on, the permission is not moved. Your own permission ends if
    you breach this license, but a recipient who complies with section 4.1
    keeps the permission they received with the copy.

    Two limits follow. A recipient of a modified version receives the Copyright
    Holder's permission in the Software, not a permission in the modifier's own
    original contributions, which the modifier licenses separately. And no
    Distribution under section 4.1(c) or section 4.2 grants the recipient any
    commercial right: a recipient who wants one must obtain it from the
    Copyright Holder under section 5.

