7. NO EXECUTION CAPABILITY, NO SECURITY GUARANTEE

7.1 The current version of VOLDBASE does not execute imported project code. It
    reads, analyzes and records metadata about projects. It has no execution
    engine, no container runtime and no sandbox, and it does not run a
    project's tests, scripts or build commands.

7.2 VOLDBASE does not provide a validated security guarantee. It has not
    undergone a security certification, penetration test, audit or formal
    verification of its isolation properties. Documentation in this repository
    describing future execution isolation states requirements, not
    capabilities. Do not treat any part of this repository as a claim that
    running untrusted code with VOLDBASE is safe.

7.3 You are responsible for the security of the environment in which you run the
    Software and for any project data you point it at.

8. CONTRIBUTIONS

8.1 Non-commercial contributions are welcome and are accepted only under the
    terms of this section (the "Contribution Terms"). These terms apply to a
    contribution only when the contributor has recorded an explicit, affirmative
    acceptance of them through the procedure in `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Submitting a
    pull request, opening an issue, attaching a patch or pushing a commit does
    not by itself record that acceptance, and no such act is treated as
    agreement to these terms. A contribution without recorded acceptance is not
    accepted into the Software: it must not be merged, and if it is merged by
    mistake it may be reverted. The Copyright Holder may also agree separate
    written terms with a contributor, in which case those terms govern that
    contribution to the extent they differ.

8.2 When you record acceptance of these Contribution Terms under section 8.1,
    you confirm, for every contribution you submit under them (a pull request,
    patch, issue attachment or any other material intended for inclusion), that:

    (a) you are the author of the contribution or have the right to submit it;
    (b) the contribution is your original work, or any third-party material in
        it is clearly identified and properly licensed, with its notices
        preserved;
    (c) to your knowledge the contribution does not infringe anyone's rights;
    (d) you are not submitting it on behalf of, or as part of work for, a
        commercial entity that expects to receive commercial rights in the
        Software, unless that entity has separately agreed terms in writing
        with the Copyright Holder; and
    (e) you have authority to grant the license in section 8.4 for the whole
        contribution.

8.3 You retain copyright in your contribution. Nothing in this license
    transfers, assigns or otherwise conveys ownership of your contribution to
    the Copyright Holder, and the Copyright Holder does not claim ownership of
    it. Copyright in your contribution stays with you (or with whoever held it
    before you), subject only to the license you grant in section 8.4.

8.4 License granted to the Copyright Holder. When you record acceptance under
    section 8.1, you grant the Copyright Holder, for each contribution you
    submit under these Contribution Terms, a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide,
    royalty-free, non-exclusive, transferable and sublicensable license to:

    (a) reproduce, store and archive the contribution;
    (b) modify it, adapt it and create derivative works of it;
    (c) distribute it, publicly display it and make it available to the public,
        in source or built form, as part of the Software or a derivative of the
        Software;
    (d) sublicense these rights through multiple tiers; and
    (e) license the contribution, as part of the Software, under this license
        or under any other terms, including commercial, paid or otherwise
        restricted terms, and including a future license that replaces this
        draft.

    This is the permission the project needs in order to maintain, distribute
    and commercially license VOLDBASE, and it is granted only for contributions
    you submit under these Contribution Terms or under separate written terms.
    It is a license, not an assignment: it does not make the Copyright Holder
    the owner of your contribution.

    Paragraph (e) is the commercial element, and it is deliberate rather than
    incidental: section 5 makes commercial use available only by written
    permission, so the Copyright Holder can grant that permission only if the
    contribution can be offered to the licensee under commercial terms. The
    grant is limited to your contribution as part of the Software. It gives no
    right in your other work, in your name or likeness, or in any project of
    yours outside the Software, and it does not oblige you to provide support,
    maintenance or further contributions.

8.5 You grant the same permissions in your contribution to every recipient of
    the Software, as part of the Software, under this license.

8.6 No contribution creates an employment, agency, partnership or fiduciary
    relationship, and no contribution entitles you to compensation, revenue
    share or ownership in the project.

8.7 The Copyright Holder is not obliged to accept, review, merge or keep any
    contribution, and may remove a contribution at any time. Removing a
    contribution does not revoke the license granted in section 8.4 for the
    period during which it was part of the Software.

8.8 Contributions are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, and the
    contributor is not liable for their contribution except to the extent the
    law does not allow that limitation.

8.9 Moral rights. To the extent your jurisdiction allows it, you consent to the
    modification, combination and distribution of your contribution under this
    license without further attribution beyond the notices kept with the
    Software, and you agree not to assert moral rights in a way that prevents
    the Copyright Holder from exercising the license in section 8.4. If your
    jurisdiction does not allow that consent, tell the Copyright Holder before
